    description: "ADR-0061 rulings 1-2 for function_summaries and library_signatures. Third-party rows in shipped built-in files (audit 2026-09-29):\n- function_summaries/*_stdlib.yaml: go testify x4 (TERMINATING -- they end a taint branch), zap x3; python django.db.models x3; rust aes_gcm x2 (one a sanitizer), serde_json x2.\n- library_signatures/python.yaml: django.db.models x22 (python.yaml:44-46 also still says the io catalogue carries django.db.models rows; those moved to a community overlay).\nWork: move them to community files; ADD-ONLY rule: a community terminating summary does not end a branch (a propagating one still propagates); a community library signature -- if it can make a verdict cleaner by typing a receiver (MEASURE this; ADR-0061 ruling 2's second column is a reading) -- has that effect withheld. Verdict names withheld rows.\nPre-register the expected move (more violated/inconclusive on testify/zap/django repos) and measure A/B before landing.\nDepends on the provenance-declaration item."  # 9386
